*Heading
** multi_abrasive
** Run-ready: two parts, the assembly, sets and surfaces, plus the step,
** contact, boundary conditions and output requests.
** Units: mm, tonne, s, MPa, N.   Wheel axis = Z.
**
** WHEEL      : ONE discrete rigid body -- bond rim shell (R3D4) plus every
**              grit facet (R3D3), all tied to reference node 3565 at the
**              origin on the wheel axis. Rotate the wheel with a single BC
**              on WHEEL-1.WHEEL_REF. VR3 = -omega turns the surface toward
**              decreasing theta (+Y toward +X), so grits arrive at
**              the workpiece from its high-theta end.
** WORKPIECE  : the only deformable part, C3D8R, material SIC.
**
** wheel outer radius (mm)     : 25.000000   (diameter 50)
** sector (deg)                : 4.583662
** arc length (mm)             : 2.000000
** rim depth (mm)              : 0.012000
** sagitta of the arc (um)     : 20.000  = 167% of the rim depth
** wheel axial width (mm)      : 0.03
** grits                       : 12  (1452 R3D3 facets)
** rigid-body mass (tonne)     : 1.943533e-12
** tallest grit tip, whole arc : r = 25.001803 mm
** grits able to engage        : 12  (within 0.0780 mm arc of the block)
** governing grit in footprint : placement 10, r = 25.001743 mm
** workpiece ground face at    : r = 25.001743 mm  (tangent, penetration 0)
** initial clearance (um)      : 0
** workpiece (mm)              : 0.048 x 0.02 x 0.006
** workpiece elements          : 54080 C3D8R  (160 x 13 x 26)
** element size (um)           : 0.3000 cutting x 1.5385 axial x 0.0300 depth
** governs the stable dt (um)  : 0.0300  (the smallest of the three)
** workpiece centre at theta   : 2.291831 deg
**
** To cut, move WHEEL_REF radially inward by the depth of cut before or
** at the start of the step; the grits already graze the surface.
**
